# Build output and generated caches — NEVER format these. THESE LINES ARE LOAD-BEARING.
#
# This block used to say "prettier skips these anyway; listed so the intent is explicit".
# That is TRUE OF node_modules ONLY. Measured against the pinned prettier 2.8.8, with one
# identically-unformatted file planted in each directory and no ignore file present:
#
#     .next/probe.json      listed
#     .turbo/probe.json     listed
#     dist/probe.json       listed
#     src/probe.json        listed
#     node_modules/probe.json   NOT listed   <- the only default
#
# So three of the four entries below are the only thing standing between `pnpm format` and
# a rewrite of generated output. Reading the old comment, a person adding a new build
# directory would reasonably conclude this block is belt-and-braces and skip it — which is
# exactly what happened to .turbo/ (#760): gitignored since it was introduced, absent here,
# and therefore rewritten in place by `prettier --write .` every time anyone ran it.
#
# WHY THAT IS WORSE THAN THE TRACKED BACKLOG. Files under .turbo/ are a build cache: 3770
# JSON manifests in a warm checkout, a number that grows with build activity rather than
# with drift. Formatting them edits the index of a cache in place, and because they are
# GITIGNORED, `git checkout -- .` cannot undo it and `git status` will not show it.
#
# ADDING A NEW ENTRY: if a directory is generated and gitignored, it belongs here too. Do
# not rely on prettier's defaults — measure it, as above.
**/dist/
**/.next/
**/node_modules/
